🟠 **Severity: HIGH**

When the queue is full, `dropRIter` picks the last entry from the eviction-target account's `transactions` map via `rbegin()`. If that entry is a batch **inner** transaction (which is never inserted into `byFee_`), calling `byFee_.iterator_to()` on it is **undefined behavior** per boost::intrusive semantics, potentially causing memory corruption or a node crash. Previously unreachable because batches could not be queued.
Helpful? Add 👍 / 👎

<details>
<summary>💡 Fix Suggestion</summary>

**Suggestion:** Before calling `byFee_.iterator_to(dropRIter->second)`, check whether the selected transaction is a batch inner transaction (i.e., `dropRIter->second.parentTx` is non-null). Inner transactions are never inserted into `byFee_`, so calling `iterator_to()` on them is undefined behavior.

At line 805, after obtaining `dropRIter` via `rbegin()`, skip any batch inner transactions by walking backwards through the map. If all transactions in the account are batch inners, fall back to the `telCAN_NOT_QUEUE_FULL` path since none can be evicted via `byFee_`.

The same pattern also exists at line ~2146-2155 in `TxQ::accept()` where `account.transactions.rbegin()` is similarly used with `byFee_.iterator_to()` without checking for inner transactions — that location needs the same fix.

> **⚠️ Experimental Feature**: This code suggestion is automatically generated. Please review carefully.

```suggestion
            // The queue is full, and this transaction is more
            // valuable, so kick out the cheapest transaction.
            auto dropRIter = endAccount.transactions.rbegin();
            // Skip batch inner transactions — they are not in byFee_.
            while (dropRIter != endAccount.transactions.rend() &&
                   dropRIter->second.parentTx)
                ++dropRIter;
            if (dropRIter == endAccount.transactions.rend())
            {
                // All transactions for this account are batch inners;
                // cannot evict via byFee_.
                JLOG(j_.info())
                    << "Queue is full, and transaction " << txID_
                    << " cannot evict batch inner transactions";
                return ApplyResult{telCAN_NOT_QUEUE_FULL, false};
            }
            XRPL_ASSERT(
                dropRIter->second.account == lastRIter->account,
                "xrpl::TxQ::apply : cheapest transaction found");
            JLOG(j_.info()) << "Removing last item of account " << lastRIter->account
                            << " from queue with average fee of " << endEffectiveFeeLevel
                            << " in favor of " << txID_ << " with fee of " << feeLevelPaid_;
            txq_.erase(txq_.byFee_.iterator_to(dropRIter->second));
```

</details>

